Task 1: "P99 TTFT spiked after we increased prompt length for fraud context"
Context
Your fraud detection prompt grew from 512 → 2048 tokens because product added more transaction history in the prompt for better fraud reasoning.
Symptom
	• P99 TTFT (time to first token) jumped from 45 ms → 190 ms
	• P50 barely changed
	• GPU utilization looks fine in nvidia-smi
	What you do
	Step 1: Profile prefill with nsys
	
	
	
	Shell
	nsys profile -o prefill_long \
	 --trace-fork-before-exec=true \
	 --cuda-graph-trace=node \
	 -t cuda,nvtx,cublas \
	 python benchmarks/benchmark_latency.py \
	 --model meta-llama/Llama-3.1-8B-Instruct \
	 --input-len 2048 \
	 --output-len 1 \
	 --batch-size 1 \
	 --num-iters 5
	Show more lines
	Step 2: What you see in the timeline
	Prefill phase:
  |--cublas_gemm (0.8ms)--|--flash_attn (1.2ms)--|--cublas_gemm--|--flash_attn--|...
                                    ↑
                            This grew 4× because attention is O(T²)
	The attention kernels dominate prefill, and at 2048 tokens the QKᵀ matrix is 4× larger than at 512 tokens.
	Step 3: Confirm with ncu on attention kernel
	
	
	
	Shell
	VLLM_ENFORCE_EAGER=1 ncu -o attn_long \
	 -k regex:"flash_attn" -c 3 \
	 --section SpeedOfLight \
	 --section MemoryWorkloadAnalysis \
	 python benchmarks/benchmark_latency.py \
	 --input-len 2048 --output-len 1 --batch-size 1
	Show more lines
	What ncu shows:
	SM Throughput:     62%      ← compute-heavy (prefill is compute-bound)
DRAM Throughput:   41%
Kernel duration:   1.2 ms   ← this is the bottleneck
	Root cause
	Prefill attention is O(T²) in sequence length. Going 512 → 2048 = 16× more attention compute (partially offset by FlashAttention's tiling, but still ~4× slower in practice).
	Fix (system engineer level)
	Fix	How	Impact
	Truncate prompt	Limit transaction history to most recent N	Directly reduces T
	Chunked prefill	Enable --enable-chunked-prefill in vLLM	Spreads prefill across steps, reduces TTFT spike
	Prefix caching	Enable --enable-prefix-caching in vLLM	If many prompts share system prompt prefix, cache its KV
	Move to FP8	--quantization fp8	Faster GEMMs in prefill
	What you learned (CUDA knowledge applied)
		○ Attention kernel is O(T²) — you recognized this from the profile
		○ Prefill is compute-bound — SOL confirmed it
		○ The fix is system-level (prompt design, chunked prefill, caching), not kernel rewriting
		
