Task 5: "FP8 quantized model produces garbage output on some prompts"
Context
You switched from BF16 to FP8 quantization for 2× throughput. Most prompts work fine, but some long fraud analysis prompts return nonsense.
Symptom
	• Short prompts (< 512 tokens): correct output
	• Long prompts (> 2048 tokens): garbled / repetitive output
	• No CUDA errors, no OOM
	What you do
	Step 1: Check for numerical overflow in attention
	
	
	
	Shell
	# Compare BF16 vs FP8 output for the failing prompt
	python -c "
	from vllm import LLM
	
	# BF16 baseline
	llm_bf16 = LLM('meta-llama/Llama-3.1-8B-Instruct', dtype='bfloat16')
	out_bf16 = llm_bf16.generate(['<your_long_fraud_prompt>'])
	
	# FP8
	llm_fp8 = LLM('meta-llama/Llama-3.1-8B-Instruct', quantization='fp8')
	out_fp8 = llm_fp8.generate(['<your_long_fraud_prompt>'])
	
	print('BF16:', out_bf16[0].outputs[0].text[:200])
	print('FP8:', out_fp8[0].outputs[0].text[:200])
	"
	Show more lines
	Output diverges after ~1500 tokens.
	Step 2: Profile attention kernel numerics
	
	
	
	Shell
	VLLM_ENFORCE_EAGER=1 ncu -o fp8_attn \
	 -k regex:"flash_attn|softmax" -c 3 \
	 --section SpeedOfLight \
	 --section ComputeWorkloadAnalysis \
	 python benchmarks/benchmark_latency.py \
	 --model meta-llama/Llama-3.1-8B-Instruct \
	 --quantization fp8 \
	 --input-len 2048 --output-len 16 --batch-size 1
	Show more lines
	Root cause
	FP8 attention with long sequences can have numerical precision issues in the softmax reduction. The sum of exponentials over 2048+ positions loses precision when accumulated in FP8/FP16 without proper scaling.
	Specifically:
		○ Softmax computes ∑130_(j=1)^T▒e^(x_j−x_max ) 
		○ At T=2048, this sum involves many small values
		○ FP8's 3-bit mantissa (E4M3) cannot represent the differences accurately
		○ The resulting attention weights are wrong → wrong output
		Fix
		Fix	How	Impact
		Keep attention in BF16	Mixed quantization: weights FP8, attention BF16	Fixes accuracy, keeps most of FP8 speedup
		Use KV cache in FP16	--kv-cache-dtype fp16	Better precision for long-context attention
		Limit context length for FP8	Route long prompts to BF16 endpoint	Selective precision
		Use FP8 E5M2 for attention	More exponent range for softmax	Better dynamic range
		What you learned (CUDA knowledge applied)
			§ Reduction precision matters — softmax accumulation in FP8 loses accuracy at long sequences
			§ This is Pattern 5 from the reduction optimization guide (mixed-precision accumulation)
			§ Fix is precision configuration, not kernel rewriting
			§ You used ncu to confirm which kernels are affected
			
