									For publishing to the audit service on a different node, I evaluated RDMA writes over RoCEv2 to avoid kernel network stack overhead. The Arrow RecordBatch buffer was registered as an RDMA memory region, and the publish operation was a single ibv_post_send with IBV_WR_RDMA_WRITE — the remote node received the Arrow batch directly in its memory without any CPU involvement on either side.
