												Key design decisions:
													1. Per-backend, per-model circuit breakers: a degraded vLLM-70B instance doesn't trip the circuit for XGBoost scoring on the same node
													2. Error rate threshold (not just count): 5 failures out of 10 requests (50%) trips, but 5 failures out of 10,000 (0.05%) does not
													3. min_requests_in_window: prevents tripping on the first request after a window reset
													4. HalfOpen → single probe: sends exactly one request to test recovery, preventing "probe storm"
													5. recovery_timeout: configurable per-model (XGBoost recovers fast, LLM may need minutes)
													6. Metrics exposed: total_rejections and total_trips feed directly into Prometheus for alerting
													
