														Key design decisions:
															1. Token-based budgeting (not request-based): one request with 4096 tokens consumes 16× more GPU resources than one with 256 tokens — request counting would be wildly inaccurate
															2. GPU headroom policy via NVML: reads GPU memory and utilization from the C NVML library via FFI — prevents OOM proactively, not reactively
